{
  "body_human_readable": "**The 2005 film adaptation of \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" was produced on a relatively modest budget and went on to achieve a worldwide gross of more than double its production cost.**\n\nThe production budget for the movie is reported to be between $45 and $50 million. The film, released in the United States on April 29, 2005, grossed over $100 million worldwide, with one source stating a total of $104.5 million.\n\nThe movie's financial performance is detailed as follows:\n*   **Production Budget:** $45\u2013$50 million\n*   **Worldwide Box Office Gross:** $104.5 million\n*   **Domestic (USA) Gross:** $51.0M\n\nThe film was a co-production between Disney and Spyglass Entertainment. Despite not being a massive blockbuster, its earnings were considered a success, with the worldwide box office gross being 2.3 times its production budget.",
